WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.310
Kanto Junior Tennis Tournament

00:00:04.890 --> 00:00:07.940
Let's make this the best match ever!

00:00:12.870 --> 00:00:14.550
Y-Yeah!

00:00:15.750 --> 00:00:20.670
The second round of the Kanto Junior 
Tennis Tournament will now begin.

00:00:20.670 --> 00:00:23.660
Three-set match. Ide to serve.

00:00:24.370 --> 00:00:27.420
<i>"Let's make this the best match ever," huh?</i>

00:00:27.920 --> 00:00:30.950
<i>Yeah, let's. So we won't regret anything.</i>

00:00:33.490 --> 00:00:36.290
<i>Because this might be the last 
time I put my all on the line</i>

00:00:37.190 --> 00:00:39.430
<i>for a tennis match.</i>

00:00:39.700 --> 00:00:42.330
<i>But I'm sure it's the same for Ide-kun.</i>

00:00:43.620 --> 00:00:45.560
<i>I want to win a match like this!</i>

00:00:54.500 --> 00:00:55.820
Love-15.

00:00:56.420 --> 00:00:58.200
<i>With Ide-kun, victory goes to the swiftest!</i>

00:00:58.200 --> 00:01:02.040
<i>I need to take the lead and try not to let 
him make this a close, exciting match!</i>

00:01:04.540 --> 00:01:06.230
<i>For a topspin shot, that was fast!</i>

00:01:06.690 --> 00:01:07.520
Yes!

00:01:07.520 --> 00:01:08.740
15-all.

00:01:08.740 --> 00:01:10.490
Yeah! Nice serve!

00:01:10.490 --> 00:01:11.840
Ide! Get your second point!

00:01:12.370 --> 00:01:15.090
<i>Wow, the cheering is insane.</i>

00:01:15.090 --> 00:01:17.180
Okay, Ide! Take the lead!

00:01:17.180 --> 00:01:18.580
Hold on to it!

00:01:19.340 --> 00:01:20.100
Okay...

00:01:20.100 --> 00:01:21.060
Nice, Ide!

00:01:21.060 --> 00:01:21.760
One more point!

00:01:21.760 --> 00:01:23.100
Ide's incredible!

00:01:24.600 --> 00:01:26.490
What the heck is this?

00:03:07.320 --> 00:03:09.160
Yosshi! Take the lead!

00:03:12.110 --> 00:03:13.690
<i>A slice, just as my data said!</i>

00:03:14.450 --> 00:03:16.420
<i>Take the initiative in my 
return game with a hard hit!</i>

00:03:17.350 --> 00:03:18.920
<i>Yes! Right to his blind spot!</i>

00:03:20.120 --> 00:03:22.250
<i>A high-risk shot down the line already!</i>

00:03:22.250 --> 00:03:23.990
<i>But there's not much force behind it.</i>

00:03:25.270 --> 00:03:26.310
<i>He's moving up!</i>

00:03:26.310 --> 00:03:28.390
<i>Damn! I didn't expect this!</i>

00:03:29.140 --> 00:03:30.120
<i>Will it make it?!</i>

00:03:31.970 --> 00:03:33.400
15-30.

00:03:34.660 --> 00:03:35.700
So close...

00:03:35.700 --> 00:03:37.960
He almost had it.

00:03:37.960 --> 00:03:40.940
Th-That's the way, Ei-chan.

00:03:45.680 --> 00:03:49.660
Whish, Then Fwoom

00:03:50.680 --> 00:03:53.700
<i>A shot down the line from that 
position was pushing it.</i>

00:03:53.700 --> 00:03:57.010
<i>Just moving up is reckless with 
no more of an approach than that.</i>

00:03:57.010 --> 00:03:59.320
<i>Getting flustered about it 
put me at risk, though.</i>

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:04.840
<i>Was it a surprise attack? 
Or does he have some other plan?</i>

00:04:07.670 --> 00:04:10.120
<i>The second serve should be slower.</i>

00:04:12.350 --> 00:04:13.310
<i>A hard flat shot?!</i>

00:04:13.580 --> 00:04:15.600
<i>Shoot! Bad hit!</i>

00:04:16.900 --> 00:04:18.400
<i>He was moving up again!</i>

00:04:19.870 --> 00:04:21.360
15-40.

00:04:22.890 --> 00:04:24.090
No worries, Ide!

00:04:24.090 --> 00:04:25.910
That serve pushed him back!

00:04:25.910 --> 00:04:28.260
<i>A flat shot for his second serve?</i>

00:04:28.260 --> 00:04:30.510
<i>And a serve-and-volley on top of that...</i>

00:04:30.510 --> 00:04:32.970
<i>It's his serve, so he should 
be trying to start strong.</i>

00:04:32.970 --> 00:04:34.460
<i>What's he thinking?</i>

00:04:35.150 --> 00:04:36.940
<i>I don't understand at all.</i>

00:04:36.940 --> 00:04:38.680
<i>Just like when I played Nat-chan.</i>

00:04:39.610 --> 00:04:42.260
<i>It looked like she was just 
attacking on instinct.</i>

00:04:42.260 --> 00:04:46.590
<i>But as the match went on, 
the meaning of that became clearer.</i>

00:04:47.060 --> 00:04:49.910
<i>If Ide-kun is an intuitive 
player like Nat-chan,</i>

00:04:49.910 --> 00:04:53.040
<i>I shouldn't get caught up in 
data and logic as I play him.</i>

00:04:53.040 --> 00:04:55.830
<i>It's probably wiser to simply 
focus on what I see.</i>

00:04:56.600 --> 00:04:59.810
<i>I have break point, but to 
avoid taking too many risks,</i>

00:04:59.810 --> 00:05:03.360
<i>I should watch him closely and figure 
out his inclinations for today.</i>

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:05.860
<i>Okay, come on!</i>

00:05:08.870 --> 00:05:10.200
30-40.

00:05:11.090 --> 00:05:13.910
That's it! Nice serve, Ide!

00:05:13.910 --> 00:05:15.960
One more point and you've got this, Ide!

00:05:17.920 --> 00:05:19.670
<i>Another service ace?</i>

00:05:20.400 --> 00:05:21.210
<i>Wait...</i>

00:05:24.180 --> 00:05:27.970
<i>Of the points he's won so far, 
he's had two service aces,</i>

00:05:27.970 --> 00:05:30.820
<i>one reckless play at the net, 
and one rush to the net after serving.</i>

00:05:31.270 --> 00:05:34.850
<i>He's won them all with his 
super confident attacks.</i>

00:05:35.250 --> 00:05:36.750
<i>Looking at it that way,</i>

00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:40.860
<i>it seems like he's just attacking with 
all the confidence he can muster.</i>

00:05:41.520 --> 00:05:45.370
<i>Maybe he's just trying to score 
on every shot that comes his way,</i>

00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:47.600
<i>with no consideration for any risks?</i>

00:05:57.470 --> 00:05:58.500
<i>Again?</i>

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:00.210
Out.

00:06:00.210 --> 00:06:02.750
Game: Maruo. Score: 1-0.

00:06:07.590 --> 00:06:10.230
All right! He already broke his serve!

00:06:10.230 --> 00:06:10.970
Yeah!

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:23.610
Maruo Eiichiro
Ide Yoshiaki

00:06:12.370 --> 00:06:14.610
<i>That break was huge,</i>

00:06:14.610 --> 00:06:16.630
<i>but his mistake saved me.</i>

00:06:16.630 --> 00:06:20.780
<i>Still, there's no way all of those 
forceful shots could make it in.</i>

00:06:20.780 --> 00:06:23.610
<i>Is he playing more aggressively than usual?</i>

00:06:23.820 --> 00:06:25.650
I-Ide, you almost had it!

00:06:25.650 --> 00:06:27.890
The match has only just begun!

00:06:31.570 --> 00:06:33.830
Yeah. Oh, well.

00:06:34.190 --> 00:06:35.280
Time.

00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:37.840
Yosshi! Time for a break of your own!

00:06:37.840 --> 00:06:39.390
You'll bounce back!

00:06:40.820 --> 00:06:44.250
<i>It's pretty hard to play when everyone's 
cheering for my opponent.</i>

00:06:45.170 --> 00:06:47.760
<i>If he's only going for decisive shots,</i>

00:06:47.760 --> 00:06:51.740
<i>I'll just have to use my 
best method to hold serve!</i>

00:06:52.560 --> 00:06:53.640
<i>Here goes!</i>

00:06:56.260 --> 00:06:57.720
<i>That return was weak!</i>

00:06:57.720 --> 00:06:59.430
<i>I'll return it with a fast shot!</i>

00:07:03.800 --> 00:07:05.070
15-love.

00:07:05.070 --> 00:07:05.650
Yes!

00:07:06.630 --> 00:07:09.650
Hey, that Maruo guy's incredible.

00:07:09.650 --> 00:07:11.660
Ide! Get the first point toward your break!

00:07:13.390 --> 00:07:14.700
30-love.

00:07:15.190 --> 00:07:16.810
That was fast.

00:07:17.370 --> 00:07:20.490
<i>His serves weren't this fast last year.</i>

00:07:20.490 --> 00:07:23.080
<i>Is it because of the sudden 
switch from that spin serve?</i>

00:07:23.080 --> 00:07:25.290
He's really balanced.

00:07:25.290 --> 00:07:28.120
I think Ei-chan's gotten a lot better.

00:07:28.120 --> 00:07:32.580
Yes, in terms of skill, he could 
compete on a national level.

00:07:33.300 --> 00:07:38.350
But this Ide kid is already ranked 
high at the national level.

00:07:39.140 --> 00:07:40.600
40-love.

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:42.570
<i>I should use several different serves,</i>

00:07:42.570 --> 00:07:44.820
<i>so Ide-kun won't have a chance 
to get used to my style.</i>

00:07:44.820 --> 00:07:46.310
<i>For now, a wide slice!</i>

00:07:48.310 --> 00:07:50.620
<i>If he loses his balance, 
don't give him time to recover!</i>

00:07:51.930 --> 00:07:52.740
<i>He's moving up?</i>

00:07:56.760 --> 00:07:58.730
Game: Maruo. 2-0.

00:07:58.730 --> 00:08:00.250
Yes! I held serve!

00:08:00.930 --> 00:08:03.470
<i>I need to keep pushing as far as I can now,</i>

00:08:03.470 --> 00:08:05.770
<i>so that I can deal with 
anything that comes up.</i>

00:08:06.250 --> 00:08:09.270
No worries, Ide! 
That's how return games go!

00:08:09.270 --> 00:08:11.000
Switch gears and go for it!

00:08:15.090 --> 00:08:18.260
<i>Be ready for a flat shot like 
he used on his second serve.</i>

00:08:19.450 --> 00:08:20.250
<i>There it is!</i>

00:08:23.590 --> 00:08:24.970
Love-15.

00:08:24.970 --> 00:08:26.450
Was that for real?!

00:08:26.450 --> 00:08:28.520
Wow... A return ace!

00:08:28.770 --> 00:08:32.070
He hit him with that flat 
shot on his second serve.

00:08:32.500 --> 00:08:35.680
And Maruo remembers every point,

00:08:35.680 --> 00:08:38.530
so it's hard to make the same 
attack work on him twice.

00:08:38.530 --> 00:08:41.290
It's one of those boring things 
that makes him so amazing.

00:08:44.090 --> 00:08:47.630
<i>I'm in real trouble if he 
got an ace off of that one.</i>

00:08:47.990 --> 00:08:50.880
<i>He's totally different from 
when I saw him play Nabae.</i>

00:08:52.620 --> 00:08:53.880
<i>What should I do?</i>

00:08:55.950 --> 00:08:57.460
Fifteen seconds.

00:08:57.990 --> 00:08:58.990
<i>Oops...</i>

00:08:58.990 --> 00:09:00.760
<i>I'll think about it while I play.</i>

00:09:01.300 --> 00:09:03.640
<i>I'll figure something out eventually.</i>

00:09:05.460 --> 00:09:06.690
<i>A fast first serve!</i>

00:09:06.690 --> 00:09:09.060
<i>If he wants to win the 
point on the next shot,</i>

00:09:09.060 --> 00:09:10.150
<i>it'll be down the line!</i>

00:09:11.150 --> 00:09:13.540
<i>What? Did he change styles?</i>

00:09:13.540 --> 00:09:15.560
<i>Then I'll take advantage of my lead to attack!</i>

00:09:17.410 --> 00:09:19.110
<i>From a shallow, angling slice,</i>

00:09:19.110 --> 00:09:21.160
<i>break his balance with a 
deep-bouncing spin shot...</i>

00:09:24.000 --> 00:09:25.350
Love-30.

00:09:25.350 --> 00:09:26.160
Yes!

00:09:26.430 --> 00:09:28.880
<i>He really is good.</i>

00:09:28.880 --> 00:09:33.300
<i>He went "whish" with a slice, 
then "fwoom" with a spin shot?</i>

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:36.430
<i>Am I gonna have to change my 
timing for every shot he uses?</i>

00:09:37.080 --> 00:09:38.720
Is Ide-kun okay?

00:09:38.720 --> 00:09:40.590
Is his opponent really good?

00:09:40.590 --> 00:09:42.890
I don't know. He's unseeded, right?

00:09:42.890 --> 00:09:44.820
He'll be fine.

00:09:44.820 --> 00:09:47.310
Yosshi will do something about it.

00:09:51.480 --> 00:09:54.280
<i>No matter how far ahead I am, 
I can't relax for even a second!</i>

00:09:55.110 --> 00:09:56.780
<i>If I lose here, it's all over!</i>

00:09:57.290 --> 00:09:59.150
Game: Maruo. 3-0.

00:09:59.150 --> 00:10:00.290
Yes!

00:10:05.680 --> 00:10:08.290
<i>That's my second break in this set!</i>

00:10:09.090 --> 00:10:13.300
<i>This might give me a big 
advantage in the first set.</i>

00:10:13.830 --> 00:10:16.060
He's writing something in a notebook.

00:10:16.060 --> 00:10:18.300
Huh... That's interesting.

00:10:18.950 --> 00:10:22.180
<i>Since Ide-kun stopped using 
shots intended to win points,</i>

00:10:22.180 --> 00:10:23.940
<i>our rallies have gotten longer.</i>

00:10:24.870 --> 00:10:28.310
<i>And there have been fewer 
chances for me to hit aces.</i>

00:10:29.010 --> 00:10:33.320
<i>Should I tighten up my shots and 
try to change the pace more often?</i>

00:10:33.650 --> 00:10:37.730
If I return his "whish" with "tat-ta,"

00:10:37.730 --> 00:10:40.320
then his "fwoom" should get a "tatt-ta."

00:10:40.730 --> 00:10:42.860
A "ta-ta" should be enough for a "wham"...

00:10:42.860 --> 00:10:45.830
No, it'd take a "tata" to get to it in time.

00:10:46.220 --> 00:10:47.000
Time.

00:10:54.790 --> 00:10:58.840
But if he suddenly comes up, 
it should be "tat"...

00:10:59.050 --> 00:11:01.340
<i>Wh-What is he doing?</i>

00:11:01.980 --> 00:11:03.480
Fifteen seconds.

00:11:05.160 --> 00:11:06.850
Ide-kun, I'm giving you a warning.

00:11:07.200 --> 00:11:08.100
Huh?

00:11:09.180 --> 00:11:12.220
If you exceed the allotted time again,

00:11:12.220 --> 00:11:13.990
I'm giving you a time violation.

00:11:14.460 --> 00:11:15.560
Please be careful.

00:11:15.560 --> 00:11:17.420
Huh? Where was the call?

00:11:17.940 --> 00:11:18.860
I gave the call.

00:11:18.860 --> 00:11:20.550
Oh! I'm sorry!

00:11:20.550 --> 00:11:22.610
I wasn't listening.

00:11:23.010 --> 00:11:25.570
What's that? A "time"...

00:11:25.570 --> 00:11:27.800
Time violation.

00:11:27.800 --> 00:11:31.720
If you intentionally fail to take 
the court after the allotted time,

00:11:31.720 --> 00:11:35.130
you lose one point for each violation 
from the second one onward.

00:11:35.420 --> 00:11:38.130
Whoa, is that Ide guy gonna be okay?

00:11:38.900 --> 00:11:41.160
I think Yosshi's finally 
getting into his game.

00:11:41.160 --> 00:11:42.290
Yeah.

00:11:42.290 --> 00:11:46.390
When he's focused, he stops hearing 
all the voices around him.

00:11:46.960 --> 00:11:49.880
It always happens when he's 
playing a strong opponent.

00:11:49.880 --> 00:11:54.520
So I guess his opponent today really 
is strong, even though he's unseeded.

00:11:54.780 --> 00:11:57.020
<i>Is he going to try something?</i>

00:11:57.020 --> 00:12:00.060
<i>I should probably stay alert, just in case.</i>

00:12:00.060 --> 00:12:04.390
<i>It's best to assume I haven't seen the 
entirety of Ide-kun's true ability yet.</i>

00:12:15.810 --> 00:12:19.090
<i>If he's not going to force an attack, 
then I'll have to attack.</i>

00:12:19.760 --> 00:12:22.670
<i>Changing the pace is working 
better than I expected.</i>

00:12:23.160 --> 00:12:25.950
<i>I need to keep the initiative 
as long as I can!</i>

00:12:28.240 --> 00:12:30.260
<i>Follow a slice serve that spins to the side</i>

00:12:30.260 --> 00:12:32.430
<i>with a deep topspin shot!</i>

00:12:33.690 --> 00:12:35.940
<i>This one gets "tatt-ta!"</i>

00:12:35.940 --> 00:12:38.440
<i>And an arching topshin shot 
followed by a fast flat!</i>

00:12:38.440 --> 00:12:40.880
<i>That'll throw anyone's pace off!</i>

00:12:41.690 --> 00:12:42.940
This one gets...

00:12:42.940 --> 00:12:43.700
"Tat"!

00:12:46.160 --> 00:12:47.450
H-He did it!

00:12:47.450 --> 00:12:49.710
Out. 15-love.

00:12:53.990 --> 00:12:55.580
Lost it again!

00:12:55.580 --> 00:12:57.800
So close! It was almost in!

00:12:57.800 --> 00:12:59.600
That was awesome, though, wasn't it?

00:12:59.600 --> 00:13:02.380
Yeah. I'm impressed the ref caught it.

00:13:02.380 --> 00:13:04.320
<i>That was close...</i>

00:13:04.320 --> 00:13:08.390
<i>He was struggling before. 
Is he narrowing down his aim?</i>

00:13:08.390 --> 00:13:10.890
<i>No, don't overthink it.</i>

00:13:11.160 --> 00:13:14.890
<i>Just bump up the risk factor on my serves</i>

00:13:15.370 --> 00:13:16.890
<i>and hope for an ace.</i>

00:13:17.510 --> 00:13:20.150
<i>Failing that, just make it good 
enough to keep my advantage!</i>

00:13:22.630 --> 00:13:23.920
30-love.

00:13:23.920 --> 00:13:26.070
Ei-chan, nice serve!

00:13:26.070 --> 00:13:28.160
Yosshi! Just one ball!

00:13:28.480 --> 00:13:30.970
<i>That was a great serve to a great spot,</i>

00:13:30.970 --> 00:13:33.260
<i>and he was able to hit it back.</i>

00:13:33.260 --> 00:13:36.410
<i>His responses are totally 
different from before, too.</i>

00:13:36.950 --> 00:13:40.920
<i>I need two more points before he 
matches my timing completely.</i>

00:13:41.370 --> 00:13:43.520
<i>I want to hold on to this game!</i>

00:13:44.320 --> 00:13:46.680
<i>Shoot... I hit too hard.</i>

00:13:49.350 --> 00:13:51.810
<i>I want to avoid losing 
speed on the second serve.</i>

00:13:51.810 --> 00:13:54.180
<i>Hit it down the center and 
watch for his return!</i>

00:13:56.330 --> 00:13:58.960
<i>That was strong... 
But he wasn't going for an ace.</i>

00:13:58.960 --> 00:14:01.440
<i>Change the pace to a slice 
without much bounce!</i>

00:14:01.650 --> 00:14:03.440
And this one gets...

00:14:03.440 --> 00:14:04.440
"Ta"!

00:14:04.440 --> 00:14:05.250
<i>There it is!</i>

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:16.040
Yes!

00:14:16.260 --> 00:14:17.330
Yeah!

00:14:17.830 --> 00:14:19.330
30-15.

00:14:28.620 --> 00:14:30.270
He's on now!

00:14:30.270 --> 00:14:32.020
You're awesome, Ide!

00:14:32.500 --> 00:14:34.780
<i>The placement of my shot wasn't bad.</i>

00:14:34.780 --> 00:14:37.980
<i>How was he able to adapt to 
my change of pace so quickly?</i>

00:14:38.360 --> 00:14:40.810
<i>All I've seen Ide-kun do so far</i>

00:14:40.810 --> 00:14:44.150
<i>is hold back on his aggressive 
one-hit scoring strategy a bit,</i>

00:14:44.150 --> 00:14:47.490
<i>focus hard, and think about something.</i>

00:14:47.960 --> 00:14:50.440
His intuition is frighteningly sharp.

00:14:51.360 --> 00:14:55.860
In just a few games, 
he's matched the timing of the

00:14:55.860 --> 00:14:59.220
change-of-pace pattern 
we worked on for months.

00:14:59.220 --> 00:15:02.830
He seems like the exact 
opposite of Maruo-kun.

00:15:02.830 --> 00:15:05.170
That's true, in a way.

00:15:05.420 --> 00:15:08.470
Maruo is the type to come 
up with a flawless answer

00:15:08.470 --> 00:15:11.270
based on data gathered over time,

00:15:11.270 --> 00:15:15.170
while Ide is the type to come up 
with random answers on the fly.

00:15:15.960 --> 00:15:20.110
He was probably focusing so hard 
that he missed the ref's time call

00:15:20.110 --> 00:15:24.020
because he had to process all the 
information on Maruo's change of pace

00:15:24.020 --> 00:15:27.400
in a short amount of time.

00:15:27.640 --> 00:15:29.650
He can do that?

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:32.130
As far as I can see, yes.

00:15:32.130 --> 00:15:33.930
But what's frightening is that,

00:15:34.480 --> 00:15:38.050
even though his method to arrive 
at the answer was so random,

00:15:38.050 --> 00:15:40.160
he was right.

00:15:40.650 --> 00:15:45.090
He's never lost at that pushing sumo 
game we play during breaks, right?

00:15:45.090 --> 00:15:46.670
That's right.

00:15:47.620 --> 00:15:48.880
Begin!

00:15:48.880 --> 00:15:50.570
There! Ah... Whoa!

00:15:50.570 --> 00:15:53.120
You dope. I knew you'd do that.

00:15:53.120 --> 00:15:54.800
And I win!

00:15:55.250 --> 00:15:58.000
Yosshi, you're good at this.

00:15:58.000 --> 00:16:01.330
Well, I've never lost at this game.

00:16:01.330 --> 00:16:02.560
Seriously?!

00:16:02.990 --> 00:16:05.570
Even the most unnaturally strong 
guy in the class can't win.

00:16:06.080 --> 00:16:09.070
Or even Sugiyama, the 
biggest guy in the school!

00:16:09.070 --> 00:16:10.580
Are you kidding me?!

00:16:10.580 --> 00:16:12.700
Even Kondo from the kendo club lost!

00:16:12.960 --> 00:16:15.700
See? Aren't I awesome?

00:16:16.290 --> 00:16:20.470
I guess you'd call it instantaneous 
situational reflexes?

00:16:20.470 --> 00:16:22.140
He can guess what someone will do

00:16:22.140 --> 00:16:26.420
based on their personality, expression, 
movements, and other info on them,

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:30.010
and instantly choose the best 
method to deal with them.

00:16:30.460 --> 00:16:33.140
I guess I can handle his slice.

00:16:33.140 --> 00:16:37.070
For the flat shot after his spin shot, 
I need to react a second faster.

00:16:37.070 --> 00:16:40.200
Or maybe I shouldn't wait, 
but go for a rising shot?

00:16:41.200 --> 00:16:44.820
It's tough when he keeps 
changing up the pace.

00:16:45.490 --> 00:16:49.020
<i>0-3... He's put a pretty big gap between us.</i>

00:16:49.560 --> 00:16:52.530
<i>Wonder if I can bounce back from that now.</i>

00:16:52.870 --> 00:16:56.520
<i>He adapted to my change 
of pace so quickly.</i>

00:16:56.520 --> 00:16:58.780
<i>Is that even possible?</i>

00:16:59.160 --> 00:17:01.810
<i>But he came back on the 
offensive after my spin shot</i>

00:17:02.250 --> 00:17:04.810
<i>followed by a flat, and my deep slice.</i>

00:17:08.230 --> 00:17:11.280
<i>How do I keep him from adapting any further?</i>

00:17:12.660 --> 00:17:15.050
<i>I just have to stay on the 
offensive until I win!</i>

00:17:15.430 --> 00:17:19.310
<i>I'll take more risks to compensate 
for Ide-kun's improved responses.</i>

00:17:23.230 --> 00:17:24.750
40-15.

00:17:24.750 --> 00:17:26.190
That was fast!

00:17:26.730 --> 00:17:28.940
<i>His serves are still getting faster?</i>

00:17:29.180 --> 00:17:32.960
<i>All right! But that was 
essentially my fastest serve.</i>

00:17:33.180 --> 00:17:37.200
<i>It might be problematic that he can return 
it even when I hit it to a good spot.</i>

00:17:37.830 --> 00:17:40.010
<i>But if I win this point, I'll hold serve.</i>

00:17:40.010 --> 00:17:41.950
<i>I can reset everything!</i>

00:17:41.950 --> 00:17:43.960
<i>After the flat shot, I'll use a slice...</i>

00:17:43.960 --> 00:17:45.460
<i>And go wide!</i>

00:17:46.620 --> 00:17:49.040
<i>He's adapting to my changing serves, too!</i>

00:17:49.520 --> 00:17:51.670
<i>To win the point as quickly as possible,</i>

00:17:51.940 --> 00:17:55.950
<i>I should use a stronger flat shot 
than the one he's used to.</i>

00:17:55.950 --> 00:17:58.680
<i>Or make it look that way, and hit a drop!</i>

00:18:00.910 --> 00:18:02.450
<i>He reacts so quickly!</i>

00:18:05.810 --> 00:18:07.890
<i>But my timing and shot were perfect!</i>

00:18:10.450 --> 00:18:11.150
He got it!

00:18:19.690 --> 00:18:22.910
I-Ide has touched the net.

00:18:23.640 --> 00:18:26.050
Game: Maruo. Score: 4-0.

00:18:26.730 --> 00:18:28.600
C-Come on, Ide!

00:18:28.600 --> 00:18:30.200
What are you doing?!

00:18:30.200 --> 00:18:31.530
What was that?

00:18:31.530 --> 00:18:34.290
Nah, that's just like Ide! What a blast!

00:18:34.290 --> 00:18:36.920
Your matches are so fun to watch!

00:18:36.920 --> 00:18:41.190
Oh, man! He managed to reach it, 
but he was moving too fast!

00:18:41.190 --> 00:18:42.180
Idiot!

00:18:42.180 --> 00:18:46.680
He's a real showman, though.
This really is fun to watch.

00:18:49.170 --> 00:18:50.820
A-Are you okay?

00:18:50.820 --> 00:18:52.940
Yeah... Thanks.

00:18:53.670 --> 00:18:57.900
Man, you really are good! You're killing me!

00:18:57.900 --> 00:19:00.570
But just so you know, 
I'm just getting started.

00:19:03.490 --> 00:19:06.190
<i>His reaction speed just now was not normal.</i>

00:19:06.190 --> 00:19:07.500
<i>Did he read my mind?</i>

00:19:07.770 --> 00:19:11.000
<i>I have the lead, but the match 
is just getting started.</i>

00:19:11.360 --> 00:19:12.880
You almost had it, Ide!

00:19:12.880 --> 00:19:14.720
You've gotta hold on to this one!

00:19:14.720 --> 00:19:17.620
Ide! You better bounce back!

00:19:17.620 --> 00:19:19.740
It's only been two breaks!

00:19:19.740 --> 00:19:21.510
Just hold this serve!

00:19:21.510 --> 00:19:24.730
He sure puts on a heck of a show.

00:19:24.730 --> 00:19:27.300
I've never seen anyone 
fall over the net before.

00:19:27.780 --> 00:19:29.570
Yeah, me either.

00:19:29.570 --> 00:19:31.520
Not many people do that.

00:19:32.170 --> 00:19:35.520
Was that play what you'd 
call sharp intuition, too?

00:19:35.790 --> 00:19:41.780
In the sense that he guessed what 
Maruo would do and reacted, perhaps.

00:19:41.780 --> 00:19:45.540
Doesn't that make him a 
bad match-up for Ei-chan?

00:19:45.540 --> 00:19:47.110
He's pretty dense.

00:19:48.290 --> 00:19:50.110
That's possible.

00:19:50.110 --> 00:19:53.540
But he can't say things like that,

00:19:54.180 --> 00:19:56.320
if he wants to go pro.

00:19:57.050 --> 00:19:59.900
<i>He grasped the timing of my change of pace</i>

00:19:59.900 --> 00:20:02.300
<i>and even got his racket 
on my perfect drop shot.</i>

00:20:02.910 --> 00:20:04.800
<i>He keeps exceeding my expectations.</i>

00:20:05.450 --> 00:20:08.310
<i>Even with a 4-0 lead, 
I have no room to relax.</i>

00:20:09.060 --> 00:20:10.560
<i>I should go back to basics</i>

00:20:11.390 --> 00:20:13.560
<i>and use what I learned in 
my match with Nat-chan</i>

00:20:13.860 --> 00:20:15.960
<i>to deal with the intuitive Ide-kun.</i>

00:20:16.770 --> 00:20:20.200
<i>Remember as much as I can of what 
Ide-kun has done up to now,</i>

00:20:20.200 --> 00:20:24.570
<i>and once play starts, just 
watch, feel, and move!</i>

00:20:27.650 --> 00:20:29.040
15-love.

00:20:29.040 --> 00:20:30.600
Ide, nice serve!

00:20:30.600 --> 00:20:32.820
Did that fall finally wake you up?!

00:20:34.420 --> 00:20:38.090
<i>I reacted quickly, but his slice was too sharp.</i>

00:20:38.670 --> 00:20:40.410
<i>He's taking his stance already.</i>

00:20:40.410 --> 00:20:42.920
<i>In the last game, he spent ages preparing.</i>

00:20:43.590 --> 00:20:44.840
<i>Don't pay attention!</i>

00:20:45.450 --> 00:20:50.930
<i>Recall and visualize everything about 
Ide-kun's vague play style, point by point.</i>

00:20:51.990 --> 00:20:53.350
Fifteen seconds.

00:20:53.590 --> 00:20:57.610
<i>Once play begins, focus only 
on the Ide-kun in front of me.</i>

00:20:58.110 --> 00:21:01.600
<i>If I can keep doing that the same way 
I did in my match with Nat-chan,</i>

00:21:01.600 --> 00:21:05.610
<i>I should gradually start to 
understand Ide-kun's tennis.</i>

00:21:10.120 --> 00:21:11.370
<i>He went for an ace again!</i>

00:21:14.310 --> 00:21:15.620
30-love.

00:21:15.620 --> 00:21:18.130
All right, Yosshi! That's it!

00:21:22.350 --> 00:21:24.700
<i>My reaction was good that time, too.</i>

00:21:24.700 --> 00:21:26.900
<i>Ide-kun's aim is just too tight.</i>

00:21:27.370 --> 00:21:29.800
<i>The shots that just missed going in before</i>

00:21:29.800 --> 00:21:31.330
<i>are going in now.</i>

00:21:32.140 --> 00:21:35.650
<i>Don't panic. I'm always at a 
disadvantage in my return game.</i>

00:21:35.650 --> 00:21:37.650
<i>I'm doing what I need to do.</i>

00:21:42.230 --> 00:21:43.400
<i>Now he's moving up!</i>

00:21:46.140 --> 00:21:47.160
40-love.

00:21:47.780 --> 00:21:49.910
Okay, get one more point and hold serve!

00:21:56.650 --> 00:21:58.910
Game: Ide. Score: 4-1.

00:21:58.910 --> 00:22:00.000
Maruo leads.

00:22:00.000 --> 00:22:02.420
All right! Now he's gonna 
show his true strength!

00:22:02.420 --> 00:22:03.460
Yes!

00:22:02.810 --> 00:22:05.170
Show us a dramatic comeback!

00:22:05.800 --> 00:22:07.620
Way to hold serve, Yosshi!

00:22:07.620 --> 00:22:09.720
Now you're looking more like our Yosshi!

00:22:10.040 --> 00:22:11.990
It's getting interesting now!

00:22:18.450 --> 00:22:19.630
All right!

00:24:00.000 --> 00:24:25.020
Next Time

00:24:00.310 --> 00:24:03.840
Once play begins, focus only 
on the Ide-kun in front of me.

00:24:03.840 --> 00:24:07.390
That return should've made it. That's weird.

00:24:07.390 --> 00:24:09.050
I'll go with a flat serve.

00:24:09.440 --> 00:24:13.130
Ide-kun isn't consistent, so there's 
no telling how he'll return it.

00:24:13.130 --> 00:24:14.900
Is he starting to move faster?

00:24:14.900 --> 00:24:17.310
That means I'll have to 
adjust my timing again.

00:24:17.310 --> 00:24:19.640
If he goes "bam," I'll have 
to hit a "ta-tat" flat shot.

00:24:20.110 --> 00:24:22.060
Next time on <i>Baby Steps</i>,

00:24:21.540 --> 00:24:25.020
Dramatic By Nature

00:24:22.060 --> 00:24:23.850
"Dramatic By Nature."

00:24:25.210 --> 00:24:31.000
End
